docs {
  # POST /admin/wiki/rebuild

  Trigger the **wiki-editor sweep** — runs `WikiSweepWorkflow` on the
  `kb-wiki` task queue to (re)generate per-entity MediaWiki articles.

  > ⚠️ **Path differs from the rest of the API.** This route is mounted
  > **without** the `/api/v1` prefix (its router already carries
  > `prefix="/admin/wiki"`), so the real path is `/admin/wiki/rebuild`,
  > NOT `/api/v1/admin/wiki/rebuild`. It also does **not** require
  > `X-API-Key` — there's no `require_api_key` dependency on it in
  > `src/api/routes/admin.py`.

  This is a **different** trigger from
  `POST /api/v1/admin/communities/rebuild` (GraphRAG community build).
  Don't confuse the two.

  ## Query parameter
  - **all** *(default `false`)* — when `true`, first marks **every**
    `:__Entity__` in Neo4j `wiki_dirty=true` (full rebuild of all
    articles); when `false`, only entities already flagged dirty are
    rewritten.

  ## Behaviour
  Fire-and-forget. Returns the workflow id immediately; the sweep runs
  asynchronously on the `kb-wiki` worker.

  ## Response 200
  ```json
  { "status": "started", "workflow_id": "wiki-sweep-manual" }
  ```
  When the wiki editor is disabled (`WIKI_ENABLED=false`):
  ```json
  { "status": "disabled" }
  ```

  ## Requires
  - `WIKI_ENABLED=true` and a worker polling the `kb-wiki` queue.
  - A reachable MediaWiki/Wikibase instance for article writes.
}
